name: NextcloudHandler
description: Filesystem handler for Nextcloud and WebDAV servers
version: @VERSION@
date: @DATE@
author: orgin
submitter: orgin
email:
url:
category: driver/handler
replaces:
requirements: clib4.library 2.5, AmiSSL 5, filesysbox.library 54.8
license: Public domain
minosversion: 4.1
texttype: Plain text
distribute: yes
hend:

nextcloud-handler shows the files of a Nextcloud account as a volume on
AmigaOS 4, for example Nextcloud: on Workbench. Files can be opened,
copied, renamed, deleted and saved directly on the server, from Workbench,
the Shell and any program. It also works with ownCloud and other WebDAV
servers.

Features:

- Encrypted connections (https) through AmiSSL, with certificate check.
- Files of any size; big files are uploaded in parts (Nextcloud chunked
  upload), so server limits on request size do not matter.
- National characters in file names, converted between the Amiga
  character set and UTF-8.
- Upper and lower case are ignored, as on any Amiga volume.
- File dates (Copy CLONE, SetDate) and comments (FileNote) are kept on the
  server.
- Free space from the Nextcloud quota.
- The password can be asked for with a requester and remembered; use an
  app password from the Nextcloud security settings.
- The volume can be mounted at boot: it connects on first use and
  reconnects by itself after network problems.
- A failed upload is reported with a requester, and the data is kept
  locally, so nothing is lost.

Requirements (install these first):

- AmigaOS 4.1 Final Edition (tested with Update 3).
- filesysbox.library 54.8 or newer (part of AmigaOS 4.1 FE).
- clib4.library 2.5 or newer:
  OS4Depot development/library/misc/clib4.lha
  or https://github.com/AmigaLabs/clib4/releases
- AmiSSL 5 or newer:
  OS4Depot library/misc/amissl.lha
  or https://github.com/jens-maus/amissl/releases
- A TCP/IP stack (Roadshow, as included in AmigaOS 4.1).

Installation:

Double-click the Install icon. It checks the requirements, copies the
handler to L:, creates a DOSDriver with your server address and user name
and can mount the volume right away. Everything else is described in
NextcloudHandler.guide.

History:

- 0.37 (2026-11-15): converting an empty text between the Amiga character
  set and UTF-8 could give leftover memory instead of an empty text (no
  case is known where the handler showed it).
- 0.32 (2026-11-15): reading stops with an error when the file is changed
  on the server during the read, instead of giving a mix of both versions.
  The handler's code is freed when the volume is dismounted (about 3 MB
  were lost with every mount). Problems that need the user, such as
  certificate errors, are shown in a requester once. Names with ":" from
  the server can be used (shown as %u003A). Files show the e bit, so
  programs on the volume can be started. Line breaks in requesters are
  shown correctly. Files over 2 GiB can be written with TEMPDIR on an FFS
  partition.
- 0.25 (2026-11-15): first test version.

nextcloud-handler is public domain. It uses libcurl, expat, zlib, clib4
and AmiSSL, see Third-party.txt for their licences.
